<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Baudouin of Belgium</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1930">1930</a>–<a href="/years/1993">1993</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as King Baudouin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Baudouin was King of the Belgians from 1951 to 1993, succeeding his father Leopold III, who abdicated after the Royal Question. His reign saw the independence of the Belgian Congo in 1960 and the transformation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> into a federal state. In 1990 he was briefly declared unable to reign so that a law liberalising abortion could pass without his signature. He was succeeded by his brother Albert II.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/baudouin-of-belgium.jpg" alt="Baudouin of Belgium" width="320" height="458" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anefo · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Baudouin_of_Belgium.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>He was succeeded by <b>Baudouin</b> (1951–1993), Albert II (1993–2013) and Philippe, king since 2013.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-belgium">Kingdom of Belgium · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Château of Stuyvenberg, in what is now <a href="/countries/belgium">Belgium</a>. Died in Motril, in what is now <a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=50.89,4.35&amp;year=1970" aria-label="Château of Stuyvenberg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4649 398 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Baudouin of Belgium"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5099 668h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5099 668h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=50.89,4.35&amp;year=1970">What was here in 1970? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
